  "text": "2:41¢ all § @\neuropean nations that are general ly\npr\n..\n-\n0:45 [2:23\nthese states were established along the lines\n\n1.0 this course is about....\n\nweek 1: intro\n\nnotes summary attachments\n\n0:44 these states were established along the lines of\neuropean nation states that are generally far more\nhomogeneous. at least the ideal type of the european\nstate, like france where people speaking french inhabit\na state called france. or the germans who speak\ngerman and inhabit a state called germany.\n\n1:04 the middle eastern states were much more artificial\ncreations. | am professor asher susser of tel aviv\nuniversity. and i'm going to teach a course on the\nemergence of the middle east that will explain how\nthese arbitrary state creations of colonial origin have\ncontributed to the huge destabilization and disorder\nand chaos that we see in the middle east today.\n\n1:31 our course will discuss other matters too, the\nrelationship between religion and state. the economic\nand social developments of middle eastern countries\nand how these have influenced the present disorder\nand chaos. we will also discuss the arab-israeli conflict\nand the sectarian divisions and tribal distinctions that\ncharacterize the middle eastern states of today.\n\n| & previous ou s¢ save a note gurse or next =»\n4\n",
